        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Bank Reconciliation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2017",
        "question_text": "<p>The cash book balance of a business is \u20b58,000 (debit), while the bank statement shows a balance of \u20b57,500 (credit). Unpresented cheques amount to \u20b51,200, and bank charges of \u20b5300 are not yet recorded in the cash book. What is the adjusted cash book balance?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Adjusted cash book balance = Cash book balance - Bank charges.<br>$\u20b58,000 - \u20b5300 = \u20b57,700$.<br>Unpresented cheques are adjusted in the bank reconciliation statement, not the cash book.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
