        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2017",
        "question_text": "<p>A machine costing \u20b550,000 has an estimated useful life of 5 years and a residual value of \u20b55,000. Calculate the annual depreciation charge using the straight-line method.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The straight-line depreciation formula is:<br>$Depreciation = \\frac{Cost - Residual\\ Value}{Useful\\ Life}$.<br>Thus, $Depreciation = \\frac{\u20b550,000 - \u20b55,000}{5} = \u20b59,000$ per year.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
